── verification confidence outside the set
exit 2
feov-record: invalid argument "banana" for "--confidence" flag: --confidence must be one of high|medium|low (got "banana") — CONFIDENCE IS IN THE DETERMINATION, WHATEVER THE DETERMINATION IS. It is orthogonal to --outcome: `refutes` at low confidence (this source may contradict the claim, I am not certain) and `refutes` at high confidence (I read it, it says the opposite) are different facts, and a reader who cannot tell them apart cannot decide what to do about either.

It is NOT a property of the source and NOT a support scale — how well the source backs the claim is --outcome, and this axis is not a positive-only one. Low confidence is a call for more evidence, so blue digs further; it is not an automatic fail

